"engenn8le13ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs are two-part verbs consisting of a verb followed by an adverb particle (these look like prepositions, but do not have the same function in phrasal verbs). <br /> In some cases, it is not possible to separate the verb and the particle. These are called <span class=\"italic\">inseparable</span> phrasal verbs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Phrasal verb  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Meaning  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" run away with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  to escape\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"turned into\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to  change\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" rush into\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" go too fast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" fall out with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to argue\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" care for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to like\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I don't want it all <span class=\"strong\">to run away with</span> me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " It hasn't <span class=\"strong\">turned into </span>anything yet", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have to keep in touch with all my friends so I don't inadvertently<span class=\"strong\"> fall out</span> with them", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He must really <span class=\"strong\">care for </span>you. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I am trying not to <span class=\"strong\">rush into</span> it.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Simple Present Tense and The Past Simple Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Present for regular and habitual activities, and for facts. You also use it to describe character and physical attributes. You also use the Simple Present with stative verbs (like, love, hate, believe). <br />You use the Simple Past to show that an action began and ended in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Note: It is possible to use the Simple Past and the Simple Present in the same sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present </span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Facts\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sometimes things just gain momentum.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Stative verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We really like each other.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Character or Physical Attributes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He has a sense of humor that always cheers me up.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Regular or Habitual Activities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We meet for coffee some mornings.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Simple Past  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">After we visited Boston for the game, something just clicked.</span> <br /><br />  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">It was kind, but I don't really like red roses.  </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "over the moon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "greatly joyful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must be over the moon, Sally!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about relationships.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to free up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something that was occupied before, available", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Last night Steve said he freed up some time to meet my family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "momentum ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the driving force or advancing strength of a development or course of events", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes things just gain momentum.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to rush into", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do something without thinking on it carefully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am trying not to rush into it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "level-headed ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "balanced, stable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You sound very level-headed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to care for ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to like someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He must really care for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "peonies", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large white, pink or red flower", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I prefer peonies instead of roses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lilies", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a bell shaped white flower", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love lilies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online to <span class=\"italic\">People Magazine</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Us</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">Hello</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read about famous people's love lives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Pick out 2 or 3 new expressions or phrasal verbs from the articles.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the articles and find examples of the Simple Present and Simple Past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a friend about the stories you read.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I read about things that happen in the present or the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about feelings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the present and the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the stories with a friend.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}